(Abstract) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 582 Td
(This project proposes the development of a School Billing System designed to streamline and automate fee management, payment collection, and financial monitoring for educational institutions. The system will provide a centralized platform for handling student accounts, invoices, payment history, and outstanding balances while improving reliability, accuracy, and administrative efficiency.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
52 552 Td
(1. INTRODUCTION) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 534 Td
(The School Billing System is an automated solution for managing student fees and school financial transactions. It is intended for administrators, staff, and students to monitor tuition, generate invoices, record payments, and maintain accurate financial records in an organized and secure way.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 516 Td
(The system reduces dependence on manual recordkeeping and improves transparency for all parties involved. It is designed to manage school fees, terms, payment schedules, and balance updates in a consistent and reliable manner.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
52 486 Td
(2. BACKGROUND OF THE STUDY) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 468 Td
(Manual billing systems are often prone to delays, duplication of records, calculation errors, and difficulty in tracking student balances. Many schools still rely on spreadsheets and paper records, making it harder to generate reports and maintain accurate financial data.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 450 Td
(The School Billing System addresses these concerns by providing an efficient digital process for student billing, fee management, payment tracking, and financial reporting. This modern approach supports better service delivery and smoother school operations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
52 420 Td
(3. PROBLEM STATEMENT) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 402 Td
(The school currently experiences difficulties in managing billing records manually. These issues include inaccurate student balances, missed payment updates, delayed invoice generation, duplicate records, limited reporting, and poor financial visibility.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 384 Td
(Without a centralized billing system, school administrators spend too much time on repetitive financial tasks and are at a higher risk of errors. There is a need for a system that will automate the process while maintaining data security and financial integrity.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
52 354 Td
(4. OBJECTIVES OF THE STUDY) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 336 Td
(To automate school fee collection and payment recording.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 318 Td
(To generate accurate billing statements and invoices for each student.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 300 Td
(To monitor outstanding balances and payment statuses.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 282 Td
(To reduce manual workload and human error in school financial operations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 264 Td
(To provide role-based access for administrators and students.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 246 Td
(To improve financial transparency and reporting for decision-making.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
52 216 Td
(5. SCOPE OF THE STUDY) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 198 Td
(The system includes student information management, school fee definitions, invoice generation, payment recording, account statements, and financial reporting. It focuses on the billing and payment process of the school and is intended to support administrative and student financial needs.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 180 Td
(The system is limited to fees, student accounts, and payment operations. It does not cover academic grading or general school administration beyond billing-related functions.) Tj
ET
endstream
